
Each unit runs the kit with its own manifest, RULEBOOK and RUNBOOK naming the upstream sources and the upstream tests ported, adapted or
recorded as `PORT-GAP`; the execution record states the commands, the kit version, the models, the inputs, the outputs and every manual
change. Tests are derived from the upstream tests, and the comparison with Pekko is the judge scenarios (S13, S14, S16 and new ones
mirrored in `Judge.scala`) and, for S11, the reproduction. Go tests alone are not parity. The Go campaign is renewed with the next
functional change in `pekko-actor`, over its final code, and its commit is preserved with the authorized `evidence/*` tag; this ADR
does not renew it.

A test belongs to the earliest unit that delivers every capability it needs; a RULEBOOK may move a row to a later unit or to
`PORT-GAP` after reading the body, never to an earlier one, and a test is never dropped silently. Restart, the overridable hooks and the
finite budget are one unit (U2) because nearly every upstream restart test needs all three.

